==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|it|VL.|*ad poenam}}. {{surf|it|a|pena|t2=pain, trouble}}. Compare {{cog|fr|à peine}}, etc.

===Pronunciation===
{{it-pr|appéna<audio:LL-Q652 (ita)-Happypheasant-appena.wav>}}

===Adverb===
{{it-adv}}

# [[barely]], [[hardly]]
#: {{ux|it|Ti si sente '''appena''' con tutto questo baccano.|I can '''barely''' hear you with all this noise.}}
# [[just]], [[recently]], [[newly]]
#: {{ux|it|È '''appena''' arrivata, dalle un po' di tempo per riposarsi.|She has '''just''' arrived, give her some time to rest.}}
# [[as soon as]]
#: {{ux|it|Vi risponderemo (non) '''appena''' possibile.|We will reply to you '''as soon as''' possible.}}

====Usage notes====
* In the meaning 3, note that ''non appena'' has the same meaning as ''appena''.

